  "notes": "The nominal capacity is the A-grade rating of the cell model, 2.05 Ah; the delivered grade-C lot has a measured mean of 1.85 Ah (both stated in the RWTH document). Voltage limits are those of the reference tests. Tester capacity columns (AhLad, AhEla) are running counters. Content_RWTH-2021-04545.pdf states both 1.85 Ah (measured mean of the grade-C cells this dataset actually contains) and 2.05 Ah (the A-grade nominal spec for the same cell model, used here as the nominal capacity because the test currents are multiples of about 2.05 A) in one sentence. Charging profile: all 48 cells follow the same ageing profile. The registry says MultiC_MultiT, which describes the begin-of-life and reference tests (capacity at several current rates, pulses at three temperatures, confirmed in the BOL files); the 48-cell ageing is one profile at 25 degC, so the main protocol is CC-CV. Unresolved: whether the characterization tests should make it multi-rate. Rate combinations (read from the step sequences of cell 025's begin-of-life, check-up and cycling files; the other cells run the same procedures; every C-rate is inferred as current divided by the 2.05 Ah nominal capacity, 1C = 2.05 A): (1) cycling: CC-CV charge and CC-CV discharge both at 4.1 A, about 2C, 30 min each; (2) check-up and capacity tests: a 2.05 A (1C) charge to 4.1 V with a CV hold tapering to about 0.04 A, followed by a CC discharge to 3.0 V at 2.05 A (1C), 1.02 A (C/2) or 0.51 A (C/4); in the CUv2 check-ups the discharge also has a CV hold at 3.0 V (CC-CV discharge); a C/4 (0.51 A) CC-CV charge followed by a 1C CC discharge (CUv2), and a C/4 CC charge to 4.1 V without a CV hold followed by a 1C CC discharge (CU); (3) begin-of-life rate tests: 20 s constant-current pulses, charge then discharge at the same current, at 0.51, 1.03, 2.05, 4.1 and 6.15 A (about C/4, C/2, 1C, 2C and 3C) with 30 s rests, listed as pulse profiles without rate pairs. Currents seen in these files: 0.1, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0 to 2.1, 4.1 and 6.16 A (1.85 Ah would give 0.054, 0.27, 0.54, 1.1, 2.2 and 3.3 C). Primary source: the RWTH-2021-04545 dataset description (Content_RWTH-2021-04545.pdf) and the ISEA GitLab page, both supplied by the project owner (source_papers/user_supplied/dataset_05); there is no journal paper and no paper DOI."
 },
